      "writtenOn": "2024-07-18T16:48:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I prefer this.\n\n`vintf_fragments` only indicates that `when system packages apex, include provided vintf fragment as well\u0027.\n\nBut demo isn\u0027t packaged together with system, so options are either\n  Option 1) use `vintf_fragments`, but don\u0027t forget to manually push `init.rc` together with demo application\n  Option 2) Use `prebuilt_etc` in build rule, so init-rc can natively included in the apex. APEX\u0027s `vintf` is also loaded, so no extra step is needed afterward.\n  \nI picked option 2). Just FYI, `init.rc` also have the similar property and also behaves similarily.\n\nI asked Jooyung, and it seems like that this is preferred if you want to put everything in the APEX.",
